  "description": "T1:  Ash (Fraxinus excelsior) Crown Reduction and Reshaping:\r\nThe ash tree is to be selectively crown reduced by approximately 1.-2 meters in height and lateral spread and reshaped to produce a balanced crown. \r\n\r\nT2  Japanese Maple (Acer palmatum) - Light Crown Reshaping:\r\nThe Acer palmatum is to be lightly and selectively reshaped to refine form and remove minor irregular growth, reducing by 1-1.5 metres in height and 0.5 metres laterally.\r\n\r\nT3:  Olive (Olea europaea) - Crown Reshaping:\r\nThe Olea europaea is to be selectively pruned and reshaped to maintain a balanced and visually appropriate form, by approximately 0.5 metres overall.\r\n\r\nReason for work:\r\nGeneral tree maintenance",
